  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using the difference of squares, \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\big[(a+3b)^2(a-3b)^2\\big]^2\\\\ &=\\big[(a^2-9b^2)^2\\big]^2\\\\ &=(a^2-9b^2)^4. \\end{aligned} \\] Its binomial expansion has one nonzero term for each exponent choice \\(0,1,2,3,4,\\) so it has five terms.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine \\(a+3b\\) and \\(a-3b\\) before expanding",
        "The expression simplifies to \\((a^2-9b^2)^4\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
